 - Precision: High frequencies may lead to numerical instability if the coordinate values become very large or if the transformation function is sensitive to input magnitude [G].
-- Boundary: The scale is defined relative to the bounding box $[u, v]$. If the bounding box is not properly defined, the interpretation of "large" and "small" scales may be inconsistent [S1, unofficial].
